# Markdown Note with Mermaid Diagram

This note is written entirely in **Markdown** (`type: text/x-markdown`).

Because the global `$codeblock` widget intercepts `language="mermaid"`, fenced code blocks in Markdown work out-of-the-box without requiring any custom markdown-it extensions or external services!

## System Architecture

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Client Browser
    participant TW as TiddlyWiki River
    participant CB as $codeblock Interceptor
    participant W as <$mermaid> Widget
    participant Q as Async Render Queue
    participant M as Mermaid v11 Bundle

    User->>TW: Opens Markdown Note
    TW->>CB: <$codeblock code="..." language="mermaid"/>
    CB->>W: Delegates to <$mermaid text=code />
    W->>W: Creates synchronous container <div>
    W->>Q: Enqueue render task
    Q->>M: mermaid.render(id, code)
    M-->>Q: Returns SVG promise
    Q-->>W: Injects SVG into container <div>
    W-->>User: Diagram renders seamlessly!
```

## Feature List in Markdown

* Markdown notes support ```` ```mermaid ```` fenced blocks
* Automatic theme detection (matches active palette)
* Fully offline, zero CDN calls
